{%- comment -%}
  The flavour rows inside a custom-box cart block — one row per blend line:
  colour chip + name, with the quantity pushed to the right edge.

  Split out of `custom-box-line` so the cart page and the drawer share exactly
  one copy of the row markup while wrapping it in their own surface structure.

  Reuses the `.bundle-line*` classes from `bundle-line-contents` deliberately —
  the v1 bundle block and this one must look identical, and Shopify bundles every
  snippet's {% stylesheet %} into one file regardless of what renders, so the
  styles are present either way.

  Expects:
    - cart: the cart object

  Usage:
    {% render 'custom-box-rows', cart: cart %}
{%- endcomment -%}

<ul class="bundle-line unstyled-list">
  {%- for item in cart.items -%}
    {%- if item.properties['_custom_box'] == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- assign flavour_name = item.properties['_flavour_name'] | default: item.product.title -%}
    {%- assign flavour_colour = item.properties['_flavour_colour'] -%}
    <li class="bundle-line-row">
      <span
        class="bundle-line-chip"
        {%- if flavour_colour != blank %} style="background-color: {{ flavour_colour }};"{% endif -%}
        aria-hidden="true"
      ></span>
      <span class="bundle-line-name text-body">{{ flavour_name }}</span>
      <span class="bundle-line-qty text-body">&times; {{ item.quantity }}</span>
    </li>
  {%- endfor -%}
</ul>
